            <ArticleTitle>Primary umbilical endometriosis: a rare entity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>119-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00404-010-1809-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary umbilical endometriosis accounts for 0.5-1% of extragenital endometriosis. Clinical presentation is typical and treatment involves complete excision. It is important to consider it in differential diagnosis of an umbilical nodule.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
